  "notes": "Capitol, Winchester pressing, per \"WW\" and/or \"\u2014\u25c1\" etch in runouts.\nIssued with lyric/credit inner sleeve.\nVersion with resubmitted master (RE-1 on Side B label).\n\n\u2117 1979 Ganga Distributors, B.V. Printed in U.S.A.\n\n\u00ae Loka Productions, S.A.\n\nmanufactured & distributed By Warner Bros. Records Inc. A Warner Communications Company. Made in U.S.A.\n\u00a9 1979 Ganga Distributors, B.V.\n\nAll selections published by Ganga Publishing, B.V. - BMI\nexcept B5: Ganga Publishing, B.V. - BMI/High Wave Music - ASCAP\n\nAll words and music, \u00a9 1979 Ganga Publishing, B.V.\nExcept B5, \u00a9 1979 Ganga Publishing, B.V./High Wave Music.\n\nNeil Larsen appears courtesy of [url=http://www.discogs.com/label/21084]Horizon Records[/url]\nSteve Winwood appears courtesy of [url=http://www.discogs.com/label/63313]Island Records, Ltd.[/url]\nEric Clapton appears courtesy of [l16668]\nGary Wright appears courtesy of [l90718]\n\n\"Faster\" is inspired by Jackie Stewart & Niki Lauda.\nDedicated to the Entire Formula One Circus.\nSpecial Thanks to Jody Scheckter. In memory of Ronnie Peterson.\n\nRecorded & Remixed at F.P.S.H.O.T.\nMastered at Warner Bros. Recording Studios, North Hollywood\nStrings Recorded at A.I.R. Studios, London\n\n\"Soft-Hearted Mama\" is for Bob Longhi.\n\nHARE KRSNA\n\nRunouts are etched.\n\nSymbol M\u0336 = Mastering Engineer [a255498]",
